<a href="/" class="text-sm underline">← Paul Frederiksen</a>
<p class="mt-10 text-sm text-stone-500">Last updated October 11, 2026</p>
<h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-light">Privacy policy</h1>
<p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed">How information is handled when you visit paulfrederiksen.com, including Paul’s Checklists.</p>
<nav aria-label="Policy contents" class="my-10 rounded-2xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-stone-700 p-6"><ul class="space-y-2"><li><a href="#scope" class="underline">Who operates this site and what this policy covers</a></li><li><a href="#collection" class="underline">Information collected and why</a></li><li><a href="#analytics" class="underline">Visitor statistics: GoatCounter</a></li><li><a href="#advertising" class="underline">Google AdSense and advertising partners</a></li><li><a href="#choices" class="underline">Cookies, local storage, and your choices</a></li><li><a href="#providers" class="underline">Hosting, fonts, and external services</a></li><li><a href="#sharing" class="underline">Disclosure and advertising-related sharing</a></li><li><a href="#retention" class="underline">Retention, security, and international processing</a></li><li><a href="#rights" class="underline">Privacy rights and requests</a></li><li><a href="#children" class="underline">Children’s privacy</a></li><li><a href="#updates" class="underline">Changes and contact</a></li></ul></nav><section id="scope" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Who operates this site and what this policy covers</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">Paul Frederiksen operates paulfrederiksen.com. This policy covers the photography portfolio, Paul’s Checklists at /checklists/, product and support pages, and other pages on this domain. It describes the website’s current data practices. The ReciproMeter iPhone app has a <a href="/reciprometer/privacy">separate app privacy policy</a>; visiting its website pages is covered here. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:paul@paulfrederiksen.com">paul@paulfrederiksen.com</a>.</p></section><section id="collection" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Information collected and why</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">You can browse without creating an account. If you email Paul, your email address, message, and any information or attachments you choose to send are used to respond, provide support, and handle your request. Please avoid sending unnecessary sensitive information.<br/><br/>Normal website requests disclose connection information to hosting and service providers, such as your IP address, browser or device information, requested URL, and request time. This supports delivery, security, troubleshooting, analytics, and advertising as described below. Checklist searches, filters, and CSV generation run in your browser; the site does not require you to upload a personal card collection.</p></section><section id="analytics" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Visitor statistics: GoatCounter</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">The photography site and checklists use the same GoatCounter account to understand traffic and improve content and navigation. Statistics can include pages visited, referring websites, browser and operating system, screen size, and approximate country. GoatCounter does not use tracking cookies. Its documentation describes temporary processing of IP address and browser information to distinguish visits, rather than storing raw IP addresses in visitor statistics. See <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/privacy">GoatCounter’s data collection documentation</a> and <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p></section><section id="advertising" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Google AdSense and advertising partners</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">Paul’s Checklists uses Google AdSense Auto ads to support the site. Google and other third-party advertising vendors may use cookies, local storage, web beacons, IP addresses, device or browser information, and similar identifiers to deliver and measure ads, prevent fraud, and personalize advertising. Google’s advertising cookies enable Google and its partners to serve ads based on visits to this website and other websites. Other advertising networks and vendors may also use cookies or similar technologies when their ads appear.<br/><br/>Advertising processing depends on consent choices, location, browser settings, and the provider’s settings. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from partner sites</a>, <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>, and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google’s advertising technologies</a>.</p></section><section id="choices" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Cookies, local storage, and your choices</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">The site stores your light or dark theme preference in your browser’s local storage. Advertising services may set cookies and store consent preferences. You can delete or block cookies and site storage using your browser settings; doing so may reset preferences or affect features.<br/><br/>Manage Google personalized advertising through <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">Google My Ad Center</a>. You can also use <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/">the Digital Advertising Alliance’s opt-out tool</a> for participating vendors. These choices may apply only to a particular browser or device and do not remove all ads.<br/><br/>Where a consent or privacy message is displayed, use its controls to review your choices or withdraw consent. If you cannot find the controls or want to request an opt-out of advertising-related sharing, email Paul at the address above. This policy does not itself activate a consent platform. The site does not currently implement its own automatic response to Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signals; do not assume such a signal changes third-party ad settings.</p></section><section id="providers" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Hosting, fonts, and external services</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">The website is hosted using GitHub Pages. Hosting infrastructure may process request logs, including IP addresses, to deliver and secure the site. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.<br/><br/>Pages request fonts from Google Fonts, which receives ordinary network-request information such as your IP address and browser headers. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>. Email communications are also processed by the email providers involved in delivery.<br/><br/>Links to manufacturers, official checklist documents, social networks, app stores, and other external services take you to services with their own privacy practices. Their policies apply when you interact with them.</p></section><section id="sharing" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Disclosure and advertising-related sharing</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">Information is processed by providers needed to host the site, deliver fonts and email, provide visitor statistics, and serve advertising. Information may also be disclosed when required by law or necessary to protect rights, safety, or website security. Paul does not sell email inquiries or a personal card collection database. Advertising partners’ use of identifiers for personalized ads may constitute a “sale,” “sharing,” or targeted advertising under some privacy laws. The advertising choices above and privacy-request contact are available for questions or requests about that processing.</p></section><section id="retention" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Retention, security, and international processing</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">Messages are retained as needed to respond, maintain relevant support records, resolve disputes, and meet legal obligations. Analytics, hosting logs, advertising identifiers, and provider records follow the relevant provider’s retention practices; the site does not promise a single retention period for all providers. Browser preferences remain until you clear them or they are replaced.<br/><br/>The site uses HTTPS and reasonable access safeguards. No online transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure. Service providers may process information in the United States or other countries, whose laws may differ from those where you live.</p></section><section id="rights" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Privacy rights and requests</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, or a copy of personal information; restrict or object to processing; withdraw consent; or opt out of sale, sharing, or targeted advertising. Where applicable, you may appeal a denied request and complain to your local privacy regulator. You will not be treated differently for exercising applicable privacy rights.<br/><br/>Send requests to <a href="mailto:paul@paulfrederiksen.com">paul@paulfrederiksen.com</a>, describing your request and how you interacted with the site. Identity verification may be needed, and some information may not be identifiable in aggregate statistics. Requests concerning information controlled independently by Google, GitHub, or another provider may need to be made directly to that provider. Where data-protection law applies, processing is based on consent where required, legitimate interests in operating and improving the site and responding to inquiries, or applicable legal obligations.</p></section><section id="children" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Children’s privacy</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">The website is intended for a general audience and is not directed to children under 13. Paul does not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has supplied personal information through the site or an inquiry, contact Paul so the matter can be reviewed and appropriate information removed.</p></section><section id="updates" class="my-10"><h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Changes and contact</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">This policy may change as site features, providers, or practices change. The updated version will appear at this URL with a revised date. For questions about this policy or your information, contact <a href="mailto:paul@paulfrederiksen.com">paul@paulfrederiksen.com</a>.</p></section></article></main><Footer /></BaseLayout>
